	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg36246"></a>
		<table width="100%" cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0" style="table-layout: fixed;">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="16%" rowspan="2" style="overflow: hidden;">
							<b><a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?action=profile;u=975" title="View the profile of Budaho">Budaho</a></b>
							<div class="smalltext">
								Sr. Member<br />
								<img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Themes/safgrey105/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Themes/safgrey105/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Themes/safgrey105/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Themes/safgrey105/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 289<br />
								<br />
								<div style="overflow: auto; width: 100%;"><img src="http://farm1.static.flickr.com/136/335973748_527d979741_o.jpg" width="65" height="65" alt="" border="0" /></div><br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?action=profile;u=975"><img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Themes/safgrey105/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</div>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?topic=3194.msg36246#msg36246"><img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Themes/safgrey105/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?topic=3194.msg36246#msg36246">Re: iran contra</a></b>
									<div class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #1 on:</b> September 01, 2007, 09:16:06 pm &#187;</div></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div style="overflow: auto; width: 100%;">so this is how i understand that it went down.<br /><br />when carter became president in 76 he made good on promises to clean up the cia, he fired bush sr. from the head, and a huge number of operatives who had worked in covert ops and counter intelligence.  this was in response to revelations about how the cia&#039;s covert ops had been involved in overthrowing democratic governments around the world.  and how domestic counter intelligence units had been used to influence elections and to subvert radical social movements.  but when this large group of people with these kinds of skills found themselves unemployed they continued in many of the same activities with private corporate support instead of direct government support.<br /><br />one of carter&#039;s other main actions was withdrawing support from the shaw of iran.  one of the main activities the former covert ops people were involved in was trying to protect the shaw&#039;s position in iran.  but without direct aid and support from the us government it wasn&#039;t long before the islamic revolution removed him from power.  <br /><br />seeing how much their influence had deteriorated since their ties to the us government had been cut many of the former cover ops people decided to use their ability to exert political influence to get their jobs back.  to do this it would be necessary to get someone elected who would give them their jobs back, their old boss, bush sr. and the actor figure head regan were their choice.  <br /><br />there seems to be some evidence to suggest that the taking of the us embasy and the hostages during the last part of carter&#039;s first term was if not planned by the ex covert ops people it was at least encouraged by them, this is somewhat speculative though.  there is much stronger evidence showing that after the hostages were taken the covert ops groups and bush entered into negotiations with the ayatollah to supply them with arms for their ongoing war against iraq (who we were also supplying),  but that the negotiations were not as is commonly believed to trade arms for the release of the hostages, but to trade arms in exchange for the iranians delaying their release of hostages until after jimi carter was defeated in his reelection bid.  the inability of carter to secure the hostages release was the pivotal issue which got regan ellected instead.  the deal was that the iranians would wait to release the hostages until after the ellection (they were released on regan&#039;s innauguration day), and once in office regan would allow arms to be sold to them below the arms embargo that was the US&#039;s idea at the UN.  <br /><br />the embargo gave the secrete us corporations that were charged with selling the arms what ammounted to nobid contracts on the arms sales which allowed for extreme markup on the price.  the extra money this secured was then used to fund the struggle of the nicaraguan contras to overthrow the democratically ellected government there.  the contra&#039;s fight was expensive though and the arms sales weren&#039;t providing enough money, and the cia started using the contras and the networks which had been used to covertly supply them with arms money to start shipping drugs into the united states, using the proffits from their sales here to further fund the struggles there.  <br /><br />seeing another opportunity to help their reellection chances in &#039;84 the counter intelligence (ie domestic) branches of regan&#039;s cia started using their informants and plants with in the black panther party to convince party officials and people in urban black communities to start selling drugs to fund their own campaigns and movements.  but the rifts this opened within not only the panthers but within the entire black ellecotrate, along with the social problems the drug epidemic within the urban black communities caused was an important factor in regan&#039;s reelection.  the two front attack on the black communities, from within as i just described, and from the excuse involvement with drugs gave law enforcement to tip the tables against the panthers in their physical fights.  it gave police the excuse they needed to arrest many of the most imporant and prominent activists and politically active memebers of black communities, while simultaneously giving the regan campaign a poignant issue to rail against in their ellection bid.&nbsp; the war on drugs was basically just an engineered excuse to launch a war against the politcal black power movement.<br /><br />and i guess thats about how i understand it.</div>
						</td>
					</tr>
